tests/ holds the spec files, grouped by feature or module (for example, search, workflow, notifications).
pages/ holds the page objects. Each page or component has its own class with locators and reusable actions, so the tests stay clean and a UI change only needs a fix in one place.
fixtures/ holds custom Playwright fixtures for shared setup, such as login or authenticated sessions and page object initialization.
utils/ or helpers/ holds common functions like API helpers, data generators and wait handlers.
test-data/ holds JSON or env-specific data, kept separate from the test logic.
playwright.config.ts holds the global config: base URL, browsers or projects, retries, timeouts, reporters and parallel workers.
reports/ or test-results/ holds the HTML reports, screenshots, videos and traces generated on failures.
package.json and .env hold the dependencies, scripts and environment variables.”